# Items 1, 2 and 3, then Item 1 retracted; then the Anchor arrives and
# `joined` fires twice. The two matches complete together and their timetags
# follow their facts' entry ranks, Item 2 before Item 3 ([LDET.5.5]), however
# each runtime's Item memory is laid out after the delete.
# `LDET.5.9_dense_order_fresh` and `_history` pin the same case in the corpus.
assert Item id=1
assert Item id=2
assert Item id=3
pump
retract 0
pump
assert Anchor id=1
pump
